1
00:02:05,456 --> 00:02:07,456


2
00:02:15,930 --> 00:02:16,993
How about this, Doctor?

3
00:02:17,310 --> 00:02:19,749
Come on, it's your turn. Go ahead!

4
00:02:22,389 --> 00:02:25,079
Doctor, I said it's your turn.

5
00:02:25,263 --> 00:02:29,458
Forgive me. Well, that was a fine move.

6
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:31,533
Now, how's this?

7
00:02:31,923 --> 00:02:33,292
I see, I see.

8
00:02:34,489 --> 00:02:37,133
Then I'll go like this. How about that, Doctor?

9
00:02:38,370 --> 00:02:39,378
Strange.

10
00:02:39,642 --> 00:02:41,098
What's wrong with the Doctor today?

11
00:02:41,502 --> 00:02:43,899
He's usually so absorbed, but his mind is completely elsewhere.

12
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:46,080
Doctor!

13
00:02:47,019 --> 00:02:49,406
It was my turn, wasn't it? Let's see...

14
00:02:49,838 --> 00:02:50,425
Doctor,

15
00:02:50,456 --> 00:02:52,152
let's stop playing chess.

16
00:02:52,176 --> 00:02:52,932
Come on,

17
00:02:52,956 --> 00:02:56,260
something's bothering you, isn't it? Tell me what it is.

18
00:02:56,480 --> 00:02:59,651
No, it's really something trivial, but it's bugging me.

19
00:03:00,049 --> 00:03:04,020
Look at the heavy snow outside—that snow is what's worrying me.

20
00:03:11,680 --> 00:03:14,878
According to the records, it's the heaviest snowfall in 100 years.

21
00:03:14,902 --> 00:03:16,617
So what about it?

22
00:03:16,642 --> 00:03:18,320
That is the problem.

23
00:03:20,560 --> 00:03:22,893
Lord Sapphire, after a heavy snow like this,

24
00:03:22,917 --> 00:03:25,200
an ill-omened white eagle is sure to appear.

25
00:03:25,790 --> 00:03:27,353
An ill-omened white eagle?

26
00:03:28,730 --> 00:03:31,187
Indeed. They say when it arrives with the heavy snow

27
00:03:31,211 --> 00:03:35,500
and covers the kingdom with its giant wings, misfortune falls upon the land.

28
00:03:38,173 --> 00:03:42,073
Is that what was bothering you? That's just a superstition.

29
00:03:42,246 --> 00:03:43,456
I am a scholar myself.

30
00:03:43,480 --> 00:03:47,169
I don't fear superstition, but history.

31
00:03:47,193 --> 00:03:51,189
In the past, whenever our kingdom faced invasion, there was always...

32
00:03:53,987 --> 00:03:56,000
Doctor, what was that sound just now?

33
00:03:59,700 --> 00:04:03,580
Lord Sapphire... that bad omen I just spoke of is already...

34
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:31,860
Lord Sapphire, the ominous white eagle has indeed appeared.

35
00:04:32,788 --> 00:04:36,286
I'm more concerned about last night's sound, Doctor.

36
00:04:36,620 --> 00:04:37,869
Sapphire!

37
00:04:38,333 --> 00:04:39,589
Sapphire!

38
00:04:39,613 --> 00:04:41,080
Come on down!

39
00:04:41,380 --> 00:04:43,720
Let me down, let me down! Let me build a snowman with you!

40
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:46,040
Hang on! I'm coming!

41
00:04:46,880 --> 00:04:47,960
*Pat pat pat...*

42
00:04:48,310 --> 00:04:50,700
Starting with the eyes... Look, it's done!

43
00:04:52,030 --> 00:04:54,060
How is it? Pretty good, right?

44
00:04:55,250 --> 00:04:57,540
It's so-so. But what is it supposed to be?

45
00:04:57,825 --> 00:05:00,820
Ahem! The champion of justice, Princess Knight!

46
00:05:01,540 --> 00:05:02,960
That's awful! So mean!

47
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,500
You're the mean one, Tink!

48
00:05:04,850 --> 00:05:08,640
Princess Knight is way sleeker and cooler than that!

49
00:05:09,099 --> 00:05:10,099
Yay!

50
00:05:11,015 --> 00:05:13,740
Haha, you fell down!

51
00:05:14,140 --> 00:05:14,900
Hey!

52
00:05:15,020 --> 00:05:16,020
It's Franz!

53
00:05:16,520 --> 00:05:17,520
Did you say Franz?

54
00:05:17,945 --> 00:05:18,945
Hey!

55
00:05:20,910 --> 00:05:22,300
Hello! Welcome!

56
00:05:22,485 --> 00:05:24,940
Yeah, it's been a while since we had nice weather. Hello, Tink!

57
00:05:25,545 --> 00:05:26,880
Hello, Franz!

58
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:31,600
So, what were you making? Come on, let me join in!

59
00:05:34,480 --> 00:05:35,480
Is it that one?

60
00:05:36,290 --> 00:05:38,240
It's me! That snowman is me!

61
00:05:38,580 --> 00:05:39,580
Can you tell?

62
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:41,700
Of course. It's very well made.

63
00:05:42,320 --> 00:05:43,920
Where's yours? You don't have one.

64
00:05:44,460 --> 00:05:45,840
I know, I'll make one of you!

65
00:05:46,710 --> 00:05:49,260
I'd better take the hint and leave them be.

66
00:05:52,980 --> 00:05:56,580
Wow, it's so pretty. It feels like I'm back in Heaven.

67
00:05:58,455 --> 00:06:01,460
It's like standing in a huge field of white flowers.

68
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:09,240
I'm sure I heard something...

69
00:06:42,290 --> 00:06:46,620
Mister, pull yourself together! Come on, mister, speak to me!

70
00:06:48,290 --> 00:06:49,560
Ah, he's coming around.

71
00:06:50,830 --> 00:06:58,500
Are you from Silverland? Take me to the castle. X is coming. Union X, with a terrifying weapon.

72
00:07:02,350 --> 00:07:03,980
Yours turned out better after all.

73
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:07,940
No, Franz, yours is...

74
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:10,040
Look at that!

75
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:21,740
Sapphire, I didn't just come over to play. I was worried about this strange noise... Could it be... Sapphire! This is terrible!

76
00:07:25,740 --> 00:07:30,000
It's terrible! Union X has reached the Orange Forest!

77
00:07:31,015 --> 00:07:33,540
They have some kind of terrifying, unknown weapon!

78
00:07:33,930 --> 00:07:35,940
The border guard has been wiped out!

79
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:37,860
What?!

80
00:07:42,400 --> 00:07:44,600
Sapphire, this sound could be X's new weapon.

81
00:07:44,825 --> 00:07:46,940
I'm going to scout the Orange Forest right away.

82
00:07:47,205 --> 00:07:48,205
Care to join?

83
00:07:48,660 --> 00:07:48,820
Yeah.

84
00:07:49,555 --> 00:07:50,840
Tink, lead the way!

85
00:07:52,055 --> 00:07:53,240
Wait for me, Sapphire!

86
00:08:12,360 --> 00:08:14,340
Tink, are you sure it's around here?

87
00:08:14,370 --> 00:08:16,540
No doubt about it, it's definitely around here.

88
00:08:17,060 --> 00:08:19,140
But there isn't a soul in sight.

89
00:08:20,590 --> 00:08:23,460
Franz, don't you feel like someone is watching us?

90
00:08:39,539 --> 00:08:44,960
Now that you mention it, there is a strange presence...

91
00:08:45,639 --> 00:08:46,639
Watch out!

92
00:08:48,689 --> 00:08:49,900
Who's there? Show yourself!

93
00:08:53,139 --> 00:08:57,200
We are X's plaster statues! You shall not pass! Take that!

94
00:09:12,949 --> 00:09:20,200
These are Japanese and French words.

95
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:24,940
Here, Japanese words mean Japanese. Some global languages are like that.

96
00:09:25,089 --> 00:09:27,180
In Japanese, "言" and "言" make "言い" and "言う". In English, it's "英" and "英単語".

97
00:09:27,909 --> 00:09:29,300
They're getting away!

98
00:09:31,009 --> 00:09:32,840
You'll regret this day!

99
00:09:34,659 --> 00:09:38,580
I'll give you a real treat. Just sit tight and wait!

100
00:09:42,459 --> 00:09:47,900
Sapphire, this is a bit strange...

101
00:09:59,640 --> 00:10:00,300
Sapphire!

102
00:10:00,530 --> 00:10:02,580
Sapphire! Franz! Over here!

103
00:10:03,110 --> 00:10:04,500
Are you hurt?

104
00:10:04,979 --> 00:10:06,980
I'm fine!

105
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:08,660
An eagle!

106
00:10:22,300 --> 00:10:23,300
An eagle!

107
00:10:23,469 --> 00:10:24,880
That ominous eagle just screeched!

108
00:10:30,379 --> 00:10:31,720
That's impossible! All right!

109
00:10:35,880 --> 00:10:37,960
Wait, Franz! We're coming too!

110
00:10:58,300 --> 00:11:00,180
Prepare to fire!

111
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:09,720
Fire!

112
00:11:18,799 --> 00:11:22,680
Silverland's castle walls are like scrap paper! Move out!

113
00:11:28,020 --> 00:11:30,620
Aaaaaah!

114
00:11:50,280 --> 00:11:53,560
Don't falter! We will crush Silverland in one fell swoop!

115
00:11:57,380 --> 00:11:58,380
(Sapphire's voice)

116
00:12:06,739 --> 00:12:08,920
So that was what caused my scream.

117
00:12:09,105 --> 00:12:12,320
If a giant cannon like that crosses the border, we'll be in serious trouble.

118
00:12:12,505 --> 00:12:13,920
We have to stop them somehow.

119
00:12:14,889 --> 00:12:17,360
That's right, we must stop them ourselves, no matter what!

120
00:12:24,129 --> 00:12:25,780
Sapphire, do you have a plan?

121
00:12:27,359 --> 00:12:31,340
Look over there! Let me blow down the bridge across the border river!

122
00:12:32,014 --> 00:12:37,020
Look! The side with the border guard armory wasn't destroyed! There must be gunpowder there!

123
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:44,120
Right! We'll use that gunpowder to blow up the bridge! What if there are X Union lookouts at the fort?

124
00:12:45,279 --> 00:12:46,420
Then we'll just drive them off!

125
00:13:04,040 --> 00:13:05,440
(Girl coughing)

126
00:13:05,441 --> 00:13:06,441
Doctor...

127
00:13:09,500 --> 00:13:10,320
(Girl coughing)

128
00:13:10,321 --> 00:13:11,860
Whoa!?

129
00:13:11,861 --> 00:13:12,861
Hah!

130
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:15,720
Yah!

131
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:19,720
Hm?

132
00:13:20,020 --> 00:13:20,540
Hm?

133
00:13:20,700 --> 00:13:22,920
W-W-Wait a second...

134
00:13:23,869 --> 00:13:26,640
Whew, thank goodness... Tink, I took care of them!

135
00:13:26,690 --> 00:13:27,520
Give me a hand~!

136
00:13:27,521 --> 00:13:28,521
OK~!

137
00:13:33,499 --> 00:13:36,920
All right~! With this much gunpowder, we can blast them with the cannon!

138
00:13:38,089 --> 00:13:40,720
The problem is how to carry all this gunpowder to the bridge.

139
00:13:41,075 --> 00:13:42,700
Hey, I have a great idea!

140
00:13:42,910 --> 00:13:45,580
We can make a pulley and transport it with that.

141
00:14:11,049 --> 00:14:17,360
Please take a short break... and come back. Please take a short break... and come back. Please take a short break... Sorry!

142
00:14:20,140 --> 00:14:23,800
Careful, Tink! Keep jumping around like that and you'll fall off!

143
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:32,620
Sorry!

144
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:39,960
Oh, it's Rix!

145
00:14:40,589 --> 00:14:42,240
W-what? There they are!

146
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:47,260
Ah!

147
00:14:49,339 --> 00:14:52,480
Sapphire, watch out! Their skin is sharp as blades!

148
00:14:53,425 --> 00:14:54,560
What!?

149
00:14:56,780 --> 00:14:57,780
Ah!

150
00:15:10,180 --> 00:15:10,720
Oh no!

151
00:15:10,840 --> 00:15:11,840
What's wrong, Sapphire?

152
00:15:11,965 --> 00:15:15,000
The mat got detached! Sol's lock isn't working!

153
00:15:16,019 --> 00:15:18,620
I hear Sapphire's voice. Sapphire!

154
00:15:20,460 --> 00:15:22,800
Sapphire!

155
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:33,220
Sapphire!

156
00:15:41,120 --> 00:15:43,140
Sapphire!

157
00:15:43,969 --> 00:15:45,040
Tink, are you alright?

158
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:46,320
Yeah, I'm managing.

159
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:51,460
Tink!

160
00:15:55,859 --> 00:15:59,650
Sapphire, these guys were guarding its feet! Sapphire!

161
00:15:59,800 --> 00:16:00,800
Yes!

162
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:07,940
AAAAAH!

163
00:17:55,209 --> 00:18:00,000
First, let me head back. Then, I'll offer you the teacher's seat.

164
00:18:00,809 --> 00:18:03,340
That surface acts just like a lens!

165
00:18:05,229 --> 00:18:07,120
A lens? This is it!

166
00:18:07,529 --> 00:18:11,640
If we use this... this valley is narrow and prone to avalanches!

167
00:18:13,259 --> 00:18:16,020
If we can blow up that huge cannon...

168
00:18:16,779 --> 00:18:18,200
The sun is directly overhead, too!

169
00:18:19,519 --> 00:18:21,540
This just might work!

170
00:18:36,009 --> 00:18:39,780
Everyone, split up and hurry! Find the biggest piece of ice you can!

171
00:18:40,660 --> 00:18:41,660
OK!

172
00:18:43,289 --> 00:18:46,300
If we don't hurry, the cannon will pass through the valley!

173
00:18:51,639 --> 00:18:58,000
With all this snow, you'd think there'd be ice everywhere, but when you actually need it... Tch! I can't find any!

174
00:18:59,269 --> 00:19:02,080
What does Sapphire want with ice anyway?

175
00:19:09,299 --> 00:19:12,840
No, no, no, being on top of this ice is going to freeze me!

176
00:19:18,089 --> 00:19:20,800
Sapphire, aren't you done yet? My hands are freezing!

177
00:19:20,801 --> 00:19:22,100
Just a little more, hang in there!

178
00:19:22,459 --> 00:19:24,960
Sapphire, what are you going to do by carving ice?

179
00:19:25,094 --> 00:19:27,220
A lens! I'm making a giant lens!

180
00:19:59,289 --> 00:20:01,600
So you're planning to blow up that cannon with this lens?

181
00:20:02,189 --> 00:20:04,100
Exactly! And luckily, look at the sun!

182
00:20:06,469 --> 00:20:08,300
It's on our side!

183
00:20:09,880 --> 00:20:14,960
Shine on, sun! Celebrate League X's conquest of Silverland!

184
00:20:15,994 --> 00:20:19,340
Behold this power! This mighty strength!

185
00:20:21,119 --> 00:20:23,600
League X shall become the rulers of the world!

186
00:20:30,249 --> 00:20:31,960
Damn it! We missed!

187
00:20:33,609 --> 00:20:36,620
Franz! Hurry! Aim for the fuse!

188
00:20:43,809 --> 00:20:46,000
The enemy is up there! Archers! Archers!

189
00:20:52,235 --> 00:20:54,620
Franz! Watch out! Franz, be careful!

190
00:20:55,244 --> 00:20:57,060
I'm fine, I'm fine! You be careful too!

191
00:20:59,214 --> 00:21:00,680
Oh, just you wait!

192
00:21:07,429 --> 00:21:08,440
Fire! Fire!

193
00:21:14,349 --> 00:21:21,120
Oh! Look at that frantic light!

194
00:21:53,960 --> 00:21:55,380
[[NO AUDIO]]

195
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:56,740
[[MAN SCREAMING]]

196
00:21:56,741 --> 00:21:59,960
AAAAAHHHHH!

197
00:22:48,140 --> 00:22:57,161
Here is the text reading "надapack" under a tree. We captured something 5 frames underground, so let's start with this suspicion.

198
00:23:12,800 --> 00:23:12,880
(1)

199
00:23:13,460 --> 00:23:13,620
(3)

200
00:23:14,340 --> 00:23:15,340
(7)

201
00:23:24,220 --> 00:23:25,220
(9)

202
00:23:25,520 --> 00:23:25,620
(10)

203
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:25,680
(11)

204
00:23:26,220 --> 00:23:26,320
(12)

205
00:23:26,440 --> 00:23:26,540
(13)

206
00:23:26,560 --> 00:23:27,560
(14)

207
00:23:56,600 --> 00:23:59,660
I must defeat them with my own power...

208
00:24:21,319 --> 00:24:25,140
No matter what, I must protect this peace...

209
00:24:25,164 --> 00:24:27,164

